 R←Test_Dir2_010(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;list;parms;buff
⍝ Test the `Dir2` method with plenty of attributes in a non-standard sequence and follow←1.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 parms←⎕NS''
 parms.type←3 4 5 1 0 2 6 7 8
 parms.recurse←1
 list←parms ##.FilesAndDirs.Dir2 ∆Home,'/'
 buff←⍉↑list

 →T.PassesIf 23=≢buff
 →T.PassesIf 7=∪≢¨buff[;1]                    ⍝ 4 is size in bytes
 :Select APLTreeUtils2.GetOperatingSystem ⍬
 :Case 'Win'
     →T.PassesIf∧/0<≢¨buff[;2]                ⍝ 5 is Windows SID
 :CaseList 'Lin' 'Mac'
     →T.PassesIf∧/{⊃⊃⎕VFI ⍵}¨buff[;2]
 :Else
     .                                        ⍝ Huuh>!
 :EndSelect
 →T.PassesIf(,⊂,' ')≡∪1↑¨0⍴¨buff[;3]          ⍝ 6 is owner's name
 →T.PassesIf∧/buff[;4]∊¯1+⍳8                  ⍝ 2 is type: integer between 0 and 7 inclusive
 →T.PassesIf 0=buff[;4]+.=4                   ⍝   We have one symbolic link but with follow←0 it won't show
 →T.PassesIf(,⊂,' ')≡∪1↑¨0⍴¨buff[;5]          ⍝ 1 is the filename
 →T.PassesIf 0∧.<(2=buff[;4])⌿buff[;6]        ⍝ 2 and 3 is "type" and size in bytes
 →T.PassesIf 0∧.=buff[;7]                     ⍝ 7 is the "hidden" flag
 →T.PassesIf 0=+/≢¨buff[;8]                   ⍝ 8 is target of symbolic link but we have follow←0 here

 R←T._OK
